# Hello

Once there was a person named Yafit who walked into a room and introduced himself with a warm smile. He looked around at the people gathered there and asked, simply and sincerely, what they thought of him — not out of vanity, but out of genuine curiosity about how the world saw him.

The room fell quiet for a moment. A woman near the window shifted in her seat, glancing at the others before speaking. She said she saw someone who carried confidence lightly, the kind that didn't need to announce itself. A man by the door disagreed — not unkindly — and said he noticed hesitation beneath the surface, like a person still deciding who they wanted to be. Yafit listened to both without interrupting. He nodded slowly, turning the words over in his mind as if weighing each one. He didn't argue or deflect. Instead, he smiled again — quieter this time — and thanked them both, because he understood that two opposing impressions could each hold a piece of the truth.

So what do you think?
Check this.
